ges(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/incidentEdges(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/neighborIndices(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/neighbors(of:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/oppositeVertex(to:acrossEdgeAt:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertex(atIndex:)","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexIndex(of:)"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdges","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/NeighborIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Vertex"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Graph-Implementations"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"IncidenceGraphView","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView.swift#L50","fileName":"IncidenceGraphView.swift"},"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Edge position ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LabeledGraph law."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"text":" it is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"text":". So ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traversal"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Connectivity"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPaths"},{"text":" and the rest run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidentIndexRows"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the view’s rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidenceRows"},{"text":", in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n + m + p), so whole-graph algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices) run at an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adjacency-list copy’s speed on every base.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Costs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is a range, O(1). On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its incidences,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every read is O(1) plus the row. On any other base, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-search the hyperedge and find the member by its rank ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" finds its place in each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over them on a base without a faster "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraph, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the bipartite structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the view’s components restricted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"type":"text","text":" are the hypergraph’s."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"text":" on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"text":" whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"text":" and whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is hyperedge ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":", with an edge ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it loses nothing.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView/edgeCount":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeCount","title":"edgeCount","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of incidences. O(1)."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/edgecount"},"doc://Hypergraphs/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Hypergraphs","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView/degree(of:)":{"title":"degree(of:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/degree(of:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"degr